{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:20Z","thinking":"**Investigating Maximal Total Domination**\n\nAnalyzing graph classes with notoriously large total domination numbers, such as Generalized Petersen graphs, crowns, and Mycielski graphs, helps to understand maximal values. The goal is to determine the characteristics of graphs that achieve the theoretical maximum for the total domination number. Examining these examples and other special graph types where $\\gamma_t$ is expected to be large is useful for deriving general patterns.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport itertools\\n\\n# (same fast_check)\\ndef check(G):\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    adj = [list(G.neighbors(i)) for i in range(n)]\\n    if any(len(adj[i]) == 0 for i in range(n)):\\n        return True\\n    adj_sets = [set(adj[i]) for i in range(n)]\\n    gamma_t = None\\n    for k in range(2, n + 1):\\n        for S in itertools.combinations(range(n), k):\\n            if all(adj_sets[i] & set(S) for i in range(n)):\\n                gamma_t = k\\n                break\\n        if gamma_t is not None:\\n            break\\n    if gamma_t is None: gamma_t = n\\n    \\n    # gamma_R\\n    gamma_R = None\\n    for W in range(2, 2 * n + 1):\\n        found = False\\n        for k2 in range(0, W // 2 + 1):\\n            k1 = W - 2 * k2\\n            for V2 in itertools.combinations(range(n), k2):\\n                dom = set()\\n                for u in V2:\\n                    dom.update(adj[u])\\n                uncovered = set(range(n)) - set(V2) - dom\\n                if len(uncovered) <= k1:\\n                    gamma_R = W\\n                    found = True\\n                    break\\n            if found: break\\n        if found: break\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"{name}: n={n}, gamma_t={gamma_t}, gamma_R={gamma_R}\\\")\\n    if gamma_t > gamma_R:\\n        print(\\\"COUNTEREXAMPLE!\\\")\\n        exit(0)\\n\\nfor k in range(2, 6):\\n    name = f\\\"Corona K_{k} o K_1\\\"\\n    # base K_k, attach leaf to each\\n    G = nx.Graph()\\n    for i in range(k):\\n        for j in range(i + 1, k):\\n            G.add_edge(i, j)\\n        G.add_edge(i, k + i)\\n    check(G)\\n\\nfor k in range(3, 10):\\n    name = f\\\"Cycle C_{k}\\\"\\n    check(nx.cycle_graph(k))\\n\\nfor k in range(3, 10):\\n    name = f\\\"Path P_{k}\\\"\\n    check(nx.path_graph(k))\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking coronas, cycles, paths\"","toolSummary":"\"Check special families\""}}]}
